  "question": {
    "text": "A sound source S is moving along a straight track with speed <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math>, and is emitting sound of frequency <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>.An observer is standing at a finite distance, at the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>,</mo></math> from the track. The time variation of frequency heard by observer is best represented by : (to represents the instant when the distance between the source and observer is minimum)",
