  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/ce199364-7d11-4653-a71b-af8e8a38b715-image.png\" style=\"width: 261px; height: 138px;\" />&nbsp;&nbsp;</p><p>Observed frequency will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sound&#160;</mtext></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>V</mi><mi>cos</mi><mtext>&#952;</mtext></mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mtext>sound&#160;</mtext></msub></mfrac><msub><mi>v</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math></p><p>Using this formula we can say that observed frequency will decrease continuously and it becomes equal to original frequency when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtext>&#952;</mtext><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>. So correct graph is</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/c07a57fd-60e2-4bb3-a803-d3878501e6b4-image.png\" style=\"width: 269px; height: 158px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
